  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 10102, guid: 0000000000000000e000000000000000, type: 0}
    m_FontSize: 14
    m_FontStyle: 1
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 10
    m_MaxSize: 40
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 1
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: 'Requirements:

    1. Read the Documentation for the basic setup of Supabase

    2.
    Make sure that you have set your RLS policies to authentication

    3. Enable
    Cloud Saving in the Crystal Save Settings

    4. Optionally disable Keep Local
    Mirror for cloud-only saves

    5. Set Save Backend to Supabase

    6. Enter
    your Supabase URL and Anon Key Api Key (Public)

    7. Enter the Bucket Name
    e.g. game-saves

    8. Set User-Folder Strategy to Custom

    9. Reference
    the existing SupabaseCustomFolderAuthResolver in Custom Resolver


    or create
    a new one: Right click in the Project Window, choose Create/Crystal Save/Settings/Supabase/Custom
    Folder & Auth Resolver


    10. Create an activated account inside the Supabase
    Backend under Project Overview/Auth and click on Add User

    11. Enter Play
    mode

    12. Login with your new activated account or click on Register New
    Account and login

    13. Now open the Save Slot Manager in Tools/Crystal Save/Runtime
    Debug/Manage Save Slots

    14. Save the game

    15. Click on Logout

    16.
    Leave the game

    17. Enter User Credentials and click on Send/Login

    18.
    Saved files should show up after a few seconds (depends on your internet speed)'
